    "result_text": "All tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the level-ceiling rule: a new owner's `membershipLevel` cannot exceed one above the current maximum `membershipLevel` among their existing household members, and with no existing member no cap applies.\n\n### What the change required\nThe new acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.coreCapsLevelByHousehold`) creates two distinct people in the same household (same last name + postcode) and expects the second to be *created* with a capped level. The existing code rejected *any* second household member with a 409, so the rule needed both an admission relaxation and the cap itself.\n\n### Changes made\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.rejectHouseholdDuplicate`** \u2014 narrowed from rejecting any household co-member to rejecting only a genuine identity-key collision (same normalized telephone + email + household), which is exactly what `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`'s own contract describes. Distinct people sharing a household are now admitted; true duplicates still get a 409.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.applyMembershipLevelCap`** (new, called from `finalizeOwnerForCreate`) \u2014 before the owner is persisted, computes the max effective membership level among existing active (non-deleted) household members and stores `maxLevel + 1` as the owner's cap. No members \u21d2 cap left unset \u21d2 no cap.\n\n3. **`Owner`** \u2014 added a persisted `membershipLevelCap` (`Integer`, column `membership_level_cap`) so the creation-time ceiling survives the GET read-back.\n\n4. **`MembershipLevel.forOwner`** \u2014 now applies the stored cap via `Math.min(derivedLevel, cap)` when present. Because the cap lives in the mapper's single derivation point, it applies uniformly across get/list/page/create responses. `membershipPoints` remains fully derived on read.\n\n5. **Schema/data** \u2014 added the `membership_level_cap` column to all four `schema.sql` files (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) and added the corresponding `NULL` to hsqldb's positional seed inserts (the DB used by tests). Seed owners get a null cap, so they stay uncapped.\n\nFull suite is green. The audit log confirms behavior: owner A \u2192 level 1 (no members, no cap), owner B \u2192 level 2 (capped at A's level + 1).",
